<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marfa Boretskaya</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Marfa Posadnitsa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marfa Boretskaya was a wealthy Novgorod noblewoman, widow of the posadnik Isaak Boretsky, who led the party opposed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>. In 1470–1471 her faction sought an alliance with Casimir IV of Poland-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> to preserve Novgorod's independence. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-iii">Ivan III</a> defeated Novgorod at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shelon-river">Shelon</a> in 1471 and annexed it in 1478, she was arrested and her estates were confiscated. She became a symbol of Novgorod's liberty.</p></div>
